.TH LIBKECCAK_K12_SQUEEZE 3 LIBKECCAK
.SH NAME
libkeccak_k12_squeeze - read bytes from the KT128 XOF stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libkeccak/k12.h>

int libkeccak_k12_squeeze(struct libkeccak_k12 *\fIctx\fP, void *\fIout\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lkeccak .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libkeccak_k12_squeeze ()
function writes
.I length
bytes from the single KT128 extendable-output stream to
.IR out .
Repeated calls concatenate into one continuous stream rather than
restarting it: for example, successive reads of 1, 167, 1, 168 bytes and
then the remainder give the same bytes as one read of the total. A
zero-length read succeeds and does not advance the stream, and a NULL
.I out
pointer is accepted only when
.I length
is zero.
.SH RETURN VALUES
The function returns 0 on success and -1 on error. It fails if
.I ctx
is NULL or if it is called before
.BR libkeccak_k12_final (3)
has succeeded, or if
.I out
is NULL with a non-zero
.IR length .
On failure no bytes are written to
.I out
and the stream position is unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libkeccak_k12_final (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12 (7)
